.TH ASPEN-MIGRATE-FROM-GIT 8 "" "aspen-discovery" "Aspen Discovery"
.SH NAME
aspen-migrate-from-git \- adopt sites from a git based Aspen install
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aspen-migrate-from-git
.I old-tree
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run AFTER moving the old install aside and installing the package:
.PP
.nf
    mv /usr/local/aspen-discovery /usr/local/aspen-discovery.pre-deb
    apt-get install aspen-discovery
    aspen-migrate-from-git /usr/local/aspen-discovery.pre-deb
.fi
.PP
Copies the per-site directories into the packaged tree, retires the
cron keep-alives, removes the legacy conf snippets the package
supersedes, stops the legacy java and Solr processes, and starts every
site under systemd.
.I /data/aspen-discovery
and
.I /var/log/aspen-discovery
are not touched. See README.Debian for the full procedure and
rollback.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aspen-site-perms (8),
.BR aspen-enable-site (8)
